---
id: smallest
title: The smallest mission
purpose: One agent writes one short text; one reviewer accepts it.
use_when: The first run on an installation, or a check that launch, observation and review work end to end.
produces: The text output `write.result`, then one REVIEW Human Task at `review`. Approving it accepts the mission.
slots:
  application_id:
    description: This server's application id (the start page names it).
    example: demo-app
  mission_key:
    description: "A stable slug for the mission: lower case letters, digits, `-` or `_`."
    example: hello-mission
  title:
    description: A one-line title.
    example: Hello from a first mission
  purpose:
    description: "What kind of work this is: `research`, `content`, `system` or `other`."
    example: other
  request:
    description: The user's request in their own words, verbatim, one line.
    example: Show me that a first mission runs end to end here.
  question:
    description: One question you asked in the interview. Add one `answers` entry for each further question.
    example: What should the text be about?
  answer:
    description: The user's answer to that question, verbatim, one line.
    example: What a Mission Manifest is, in three sentences.
  done_means:
    description: What the user said finished looks like, verbatim, one line.
    example: I read three clear sentences and approve them.
  out_of_scope:
    description: What the user ruled out, verbatim, one line. Delete the `out_of_scope` entry when they ruled out nothing.
    example: No web research.
  goal:
    description: The outcome in the user's words, one line.
    example: Write three sentences that explain what a Mission Manifest is.
  criterion:
    description: How the reviewer knows it is done, one line.
    example: The text is three sentences and names compile, submit and start.
  model_profile:
    description: A Model Profile the lane routes (topic `models`).
    example: producer.default
  sandbox_profile:
    description: A sandbox profile bound on this installation (topic `manifest`).
    example: research.standard
  budget_usd:
    description: The ceiling on model spend in US dollars, a number.
    example: "0.5"
  reviewer:
    description: Who resolves the review; an actor id, or a reviewer role such as `owner`. To resolve it yourself write your own actor id, the `resolution.actor_ref` of a compile report.
    example: owner
notes:
  - The run stops at `review` and waits. Its inbox notification is `review_required`. Only the named reviewer can resolve the Human Task (that actor, or a principal holding `reviewer:<role>`); anyone else is refused `not_reviewer`.
  - The agent submits through the `submit_output` tool, pinned at its latest admitted revision.
  - The `brief` block is the interview's result in the user's words. Every node is told the purpose, the request, what done means, what it was given and each criterion whose `evidence` names an output it owes, so an `instruction` holds the task alone.
---
manifest: mission/v2
mission:
  key: {{mission_key}}
  application: {{application_id}}
  title: >-
    {{title}}
  description: >-
    {{goal}}
  brief:
    purpose: {{purpose}}
    request: >-
      {{request}}
    answers:
      - question: >-
          {{question}}
        answer: >-
          {{answer}}
    done_means: >-
      {{done_means}}
    out_of_scope:
      - >-
        {{out_of_scope}}
  goals:
    - key: result
      description: >-
        {{goal}}
      importance: primary
      objectives:
        - key: write_result
          description: Write the text and submit it as the output named result.
      criteria:
        - key: accepted
          description: >-
            {{criterion}}
          evidence: [result]
          acceptance:
            human: review_accept
  environment:
    lane: deep_agents
    model:
      profile: {{model_profile}}
    sandbox:
      profile: {{sandbox_profile}}
    capabilities:
      - pin: tool.knowledge-submit-output@latest
        kind: tool
        as: submit_output
    budget:
      usd: {{budget_usd}}
      tokens: 150000
      wall_clock: 15m
      tool_calls: 8
    governors:
      depth: 1
      fan_out: 1
      iterations: 1
      patience: 1
    side_effects: [read_only, workspace_write]
  program:
    key: root
    behavior: stage_graph
    objectives: [result]
    nodes:
      - key: write
        behavior: agent_executor
        objectives: [write_result]
        instruction: >-
          {{goal}}
          Submit the text as "write.result" with the submit_output tool, as one inline text item.
        outputs:
          - name: result
            form: text
            media_type: text/plain
      - key: review
        behavior: human_gate
        objectives: [result]
        depends_on: [write]
        task:
          kind: REVIEW
          prompt: >-
            {{criterion}}
          reviewers: [{{reviewer}}]
          packet: [write.result]
          on_timeout: keep_waiting
  controls:
    commands_allowed: [pause, resume, cancel, queue_instruction, add_context]
